 "scope": [
  "Detects: frame-timing or clock-map errors of one frame or more (shift controls), flipped or transposed geometry (mirror control), grossly wrong pixel mapping, and missing or displaced chunks.",
  "Does not detect: contrast-threshold or noise mismatch (count magnitudes cancel in the NCC), sub-frame timing errors much smaller than one APS interval, or v2e's timestamp pyramid within a frame interval.",
  "Scene dependence: the shift controls stay high when the scene moves slowly between frames (outdoor driving at low speed, D-029), so their margin below the aligned NCC is the evidence, not their absolute value; indoor flying scenes have sparser texture and faster rotation, so their NCC level is not comparable with outdoor_day2 in absolute terms."
